  "howNicotineTitle": "How the nicotine estimate is calculated",
  "howNicotineBody": "Each cigarette is assumed to deliver about 1.2 mg of absorbed nicotine (a published range of roughly 1–1.5 mg). Your estimated exposure curve sums every cigarette you log and halves that total every 2 hours — nicotine's typical plasma half-life. The screen shows a 0–100 normalised curve, never an absolute blood level.",
  "howNicotineLimits": "Limits: this is a behavioural model, not a measurement. Absorption varies with how you smoke, the product and your metabolism. Nothing in this app is measured from your body.",
  "howNicotineSources": "Sources: Benowitz, NEJM 2010 (nicotine absorption 1–1.5 mg/cigarette); Hukkanen et al., Pharmacol Rev 2005 (plasma half-life ~2 h).",
  "howWeeksTitle": "How the weeks estimate is calculated",
  "howWeeksBody": "We compare the average of your last 7 days with your weekly reduction rate and solve for when your daily budget reaches the final-week level. The result is always a range, updated weekly — never a fixed date.",
  "howSavingsTitle": "How savings are calculated",
  "howSavingsBody": "Your pack price divided by cigarettes per pack gives a per-cigarette cost. Cigarettes you avoid relative to your baseline multiply that cost. Prices you enter stay on your device.",
  "howTitle": "How this estimate is calculated",
